WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.138
The pictures on your frog worksheet are mixed up.

00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:04.625
Let us put them into order.

00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:06.000
First come the eggs.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.988
A tadpole hatches from an egg.

00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:13.587
In this life cycle, the tadpole is an early stage of the frog, not a baby tiger.

00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:19.150
Even if an answer has been circled on a worksheet, we must check it against what the animal actually does.

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:24.008
A tadpole has a tail and looks different from an adult frog.

00:00:24.008 --> 00:00:29.921
As it develops legs and its tail becomes shorter, it reaches the froglet stage.

00:00:29.921 --> 00:00:34.196
The froglet in your picture has legs and still has a small tail.

00:00:34.196 --> 00:00:35.971
Then it becomes an adult frog.

00:00:35.971 --> 00:00:40.496
Our four stages are eggs, tadpole, froglet and adult frog.

00:00:40.496 --> 00:00:43.796
The young frog does not turn into a new kind of animal.

00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:47.996
A butterfly begins life as an egg.

00:00:47.996 --> 00:00:50.421
The egg hatches into a caterpillar.

00:00:50.421 --> 00:00:56.058
The caterpillar grows, then develops into a chrysalis, also called the pupa stage.

00:00:56.058 --> 00:01:00.608
The change continues inside, and an adult butterfly emerges.

00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:03.571
The caterpillar looks different from the adult butterfly.

00:01:03.571 --> 00:01:06.933
It is not a miniature butterfly with tiny wings.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.796
It is the young stage of that same kind of animal.

00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:15.683
Compare a caterpillar with an adult butterfly, or a tadpole with an adult frog.

00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:18.271
Their shapes and ways of moving are different.

00:01:18.271 --> 00:01:20.383
Yet the life cycle connects them.

00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:25.258
A picture alone may surprise you, so use the sequence as evidence.

00:01:25.258 --> 00:01:30.371
On your worksheet you may draw any two butterfly stages and label them correctly.

00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:36.133
There are four stages in the full cycle, even though the task asks you to draw only two.

00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:43.833
Try saying the frog sequence without looking: eggs, tadpole, froglet, adult frog.

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:49.983
Now try the butterfly sequence: egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, adult butterfly.

00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:55.221
In the activity you can rebuild both cycles and draw two stages.

00:01:55.221 --> 00:01:56.896
Take the time you need to think.

00:01:56.896 --> 00:02:02.358
We keep the explanation moving, but you control the pause button when you want to examine a change.
